From: Baolin Zhu <zhubaolin@zju.edu.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Re-check upstream after stage 2

Stage 2 can copy a foreign Archive-Update-in-Progress file that
appeared while it was running. The old check runs only before stage 2,
so that file was published and the run still exited 0 and wrote a
trace.

Look again after a successful stage 2. A foreign file takes the same
retry path as a pre-stage2 hit: sleep UIPSLEEP and rerun from stage 1,
sharing the UIPRETRIES counter. The trace is written only after a
stage 2 that leaves no foreign file. When the retries run out the
script exits with an error and writes no trace.

Applies to archvsync master (6533577), independently of
archvsync-container-logging.patch.
---
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 009ded8..507e881 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -110,6 +110,15 @@ When the script receives a second push while it is running and syncing
 the archive it won't ignore it. Instead it will rerun the
 synchronisation step to ensure the archive is correctly synchronised.
 
+The same applies when the upstream mirror itself starts an update during
+our run. A foreign `Archive-Update-in-Progress-*` file is checked before
+stage 2 and again after stage 2. Stage 2 can copy one that appeared
+while it was running; accepting that tree would publish indexes from
+the middle of the upstream push. The run is retried from stage 1, and
+the trace file is written only once stage 2 finishes with no such file
+left. If the retries run out, the script exits with an error and writes
+no trace.
+
 Scripts that fail to do that risk ending up with an inconsistent archive.
 
 ### Can do multi-stage archive synchronisations
diff --git a/bin/ftpsync b/bin/ftpsync
index 25cefe5..fd65587 100755
--- a/bin/ftpsync
+++ b/bin/ftpsync
@@ -135,6 +135,58 @@ run_rsync() {
     >>"${LOG_RSYNC_ERROR}" 2>&1 || return $?
 }
 
+# Look for an upstream Archive-Update-in-Progress file in $TO.
+#
+# Our own lock is ignored. A foreign AUIP means upstream started (or was
+# still in) an update that overlaps this run. Such a file is deleted: if
+# upstream is still updating, the next rsync will copy it again.
+#
+# Sets upstream_uip=true when one was found, false otherwise.
+detect_upstream_uip() {
+    upstream_uip=false
+    for aupfile in "${TO}/Archive-Update-in-Progress-"*; do
+        case "$aupfile" in
+            "${TO}/Archive-Update-in-Progress-*")
+                error "Lock file is missing, this should not happen"
+                ;;
+            "${LOCK}")
+                :
+                ;;
+            *)
+                if [[ -f $aupfile ]]; then
+                    # Remove the file, it will be synced again if
+                    # upstream is still not done
+                    rm -f "$aupfile"
+                else
+                    log "AUIP file '$aupfile' is not really a file, weird"
+                fi
+                upstream_uip=true
+                ;;
+        esac
+    done
+}
+
+# Upstream was updating. Sleep and retry while we still have attempts,
+# otherwise fail this sync. A retry re-runs stage1 before stage2, so the
+# tree is fetched again against a quiet upstream.
+#
+# Leaves result=0 when a retry was scheduled, result=1 when giving up.
+# The caller must not write a trace while a retry is pending or after
+# this gives up: the tree was copied while upstream was mid-update.
+defer_or_abort_for_upstream_uip() {
+    if [[ ${UPDATE_RETRIES} -lt ${UIPRETRIES} ]]; then
+        log "Retrying update in ${UIPSLEEP}"
+        touch "${UPDATEREQUIRED}"
+        UPDATE_RETRIES=$(($UPDATE_RETRIES+1))
+        sleep "${UIPSLEEP}"
+        result=0
+    else
+        error "Update has been retried ${UPDATE_RETRIES} times, aborting"
+        log "Perhaps upstream is still updating or there's a stale AUIP file"
+        result=1
+    fi
+}
+
 # Check rsyncs return value
 check_rsync() {
     ret=$1
@@ -657,41 +709,11 @@ while [[ -e ${UPDATEREQUIRED} ]]; do
 
     # if we want stage2 *or* all
     if [[ true = ${SYNCSTAGE2} ]] || [[ true = ${SYNCALL} ]]; then
-        upstream_uip=false
-        for aupfile in "${TO}/Archive-Update-in-Progress-"*; do
-            case "$aupfile" in
-                "${TO}/Archive-Update-in-Progress-*")
-                    error "Lock file is missing, this should not happen"
-                    ;;
-                "${LOCK}")
-                    :
-                    ;;
-                *)
-                    if [[ -f $aupfile ]]; then
-                        # Remove the file, it will be synced again if
-                        # upstream is still not done
-                        rm -f "$aupfile"
-                    else
-                        log "AUIP file '$aupfile' is not really a file, weird"
-                    fi
-                    upstream_uip=true
-                    ;;
-            esac
-        done
+        detect_upstream_uip
 
         if [[ true = ${upstream_uip} ]]; then
             log "Upstream archive update in progress, skipping stage2"
-            if [[ ${UPDATE_RETRIES} -lt ${UIPRETRIES} ]]; then
-                log "Retrying update in ${UIPSLEEP}"
-                touch "${UPDATEREQUIRED}"
-                UPDATE_RETRIES=$(($UPDATE_RETRIES+1))
-                sleep "${UIPSLEEP}"
-                result=0
-            else
-                error "Update has been retried ${UPDATE_RETRIES} times, aborting"
-                log "Perhaps upstream is still updating or there's a stale AUIP file"
-                result=1
-            fi
+            defer_or_abort_for_upstream_uip
         else
             # We are lucky, it worked. Now do step 2 and sync again, this time including
             # the packages/releases files
@@ -702,6 +724,20 @@ while [[ -e ${UPDATEREQUIRED} ]]; do
             STATS_TOTAL_RSYNC_TIME2=$(( STATS_TOTAL_RSYNC_TIME2 + rsync_ended - rsync_started ))
 
             log "Back from rsync with returncode ${result}"
+
+            # Stage2 itself can copy a foreign AUIP. Upstream may have
+            # started a push after the check above, and a long stage2
+            # then publishes indexes from the middle of that push.
+            # Treat that the same as a pre-stage2 hit: do not accept
+            # this run. The trace is written only after the loop, once
+            # no foreign AUIP remains.
+            if [[ ${result} -eq 0 ]] || [[ ${result} -eq 24 ]]; then
+                detect_upstream_uip
+                if [[ true = ${upstream_uip} ]]; then
+                    log "Upstream archive update in progress after stage2, not accepting this sync"
+                    defer_or_abort_for_upstream_uip
+                fi
+            fi
         fi
     else
         # Fake a good resultcode
diff --git a/doc/ftpsync.conf.5.md b/doc/ftpsync.conf.5.md
index 120f7ad..96c2dc5 100644
--- a/doc/ftpsync.conf.5.md
+++ b/doc/ftpsync.conf.5.md
@@ -218,13 +218,23 @@ These options can be used to include or exclude specified architectures or other
 
 **UIPSLEEP**
 :   Number of seconds to sleep before retrying to sync whenever upstream
-    is found to be updating while our update is running
+    is found to be updating while our update is running.
+
+    Upstream is considered to be updating when a foreign
+    `Archive-Update-in-Progress-*` file is present. That check runs
+    before stage 2 and again after a successful stage 2: stage 2 can
+    copy such a file if upstream starts a push while it is running.
+    Either hit skips accepting the tree. The foreign file is removed
+    and the whole sync is retried after this delay, so stage 1 runs
+    again before the next stage 2. The trace file is written only
+    after a stage 2 that leaves no foreign file behind.
 
     Default: **1200**
 
 **UIPRETRIES**
 :   Number of times the update operation will be retried when upstream
-    is found to be updating while our update is running.
+    is found to be updating while our update is running. Hits before
+    stage 2 and hits discovered after stage 2 share this counter.
     Note that these are retries, so: 1st attempt + retries = total attempts
 
     Default: **3**
